-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived material and where it lives
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

bastet-cc/detectors/*.md
    The 56 detection prompts in this directory are OneSavie Lab's work, extracted
    verbatim from the `chainLlm` nodes of the nine n8n workflow JSON files in
    upstream Bastet's `n8n_workflow/`. Prompt text is unmodified. The YAML front
    matter above each prompt (id, name, source_workflow, tags, routing_hints,
    prompt_chars) is ours and is not part of the upstream work.
    Extraction is reproducible: bastet-cc/scripts/extract_detectors.py

bastet_cc/evaluate.py :: upstream_sample, upstream_score
    A deliberate behavioural reimplementation of upstream's
    cli/commands/evaluate/eval.py, including its defects, so that predictions can
    be scored under upstream's own rules. Written from the published source, not
    copied from it. Upstream line numbers are cited in comments to make the
    correspondence auditable.

bastet_cc/plan.py :: _plan_broadcast
    A behavioural reimplementation of upstream's cli/commands/scan/scan.py file
    enumeration, serving as the experimental control arm. Two deviations are
    documented in the module docstring.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not covered by this licence
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Corpus and labels
    The smart-contract corpus and the labelled findings come from the Bastet
    Kaggle competition (`onesavie-bastet`, 1 April - 1 July 2026), labelled by
    DeFiHackLabs. They are NOT redistributed here: the competition's terms for
    redistributing labelled findings are not stated anywhere we could find, so
    the CSVs and the extracted repositories stay local. bastet-cc/README.md
    documents how to fetch them from the original source.

"Tag Definitions.md"
    The tag taxonomy is OneSavie Lab's, reproduced from their public Notion page
    (linked at the top of the file) because the synthesis pipeline reads it as
    input. It is documentation, not code, and is included under the same
    attribution as the detectors.

bastet-cc/detectors_synth/*.md
    Ours. Induced from the labelled corpus by bastet_cc/synth/; no upstream
    prompt text is reused.
